   "reason": "[\"Category not decided by the shared analysis: the order is a section 4(a)-type interim agreement pending code approval, not a section 3(a) approval; no held source shows how S.J. Res. 113 section 2 (which repealed code approval and enforcement provisions) reached such an agreement.\", \"Own terms give several different ends that need held dates: the agreement binds \\\"pending the approval of a Code of Fair Competition for the Industry\\\", the footing-equipment term runs \\\"until the date on which the Code shall go into effect\\\", and the knitting-shift allowance runs \\\"until December 31, 1933\\\". A held order approves a Code of Fair Competition for the Hosiery Industry (EO 6258-C, August 26, 1933), but no held text says it is the code this agreement awaited, and the code's effective date is not held.\", \"The order is also subject to cancellation or modification at any time, and no held record shows whether the government cancelled or modified it before the code took effect. The single machine clause also merges the hours, wages, employer-rights and cancellation terms, which need separate ends.\"]"
  },
